{
	"VersionNumber": 1,
	"ResourceName": "okta_user_allowlist",
	"Description": "Tuning control for $OKTA_TUNING: suppress Okta detections involving accounts you have vouched for, whether the account is the actor or the target. A row that is enabled and unexpired drops the event outright.\n\nFields: key,enabled,until_ymd,reason\n  - key: the lower-cased username with the email domain stripped, matched against both actorUserNorm and targetUserNorm (so bob@example.com is keyed as bob)\n  - enabled: 1 to apply the row, 0 to park it without deleting it\n  - until_ymd: YYYYMMDD expiry, compared against the event's published date; leave empty for a permanent exception\n  - reason: free text, so the next analyst knows why the exception exists\n\nCurrent contents:\nkey,enabled,until_ymd,reason\nsvc-okta-sync,1,,directory sync service account - permanently allowed\nalice,1,20261231,tenant migration exception - allowed until end of 2026\n\nUsage:\n$OKTA_RISK_SCORE\n$OKTA_TUNING",
